"""
SoC-corrected fuel of a drive-cycle run: the fuel the engine burned, plus the fuel it would take
to put back the energy the battery's store gave up, both per 100 km of distance driven.

    m_fuel = ∫ mdot_fuel dt        E_batt = ∫ P_stored dt        s = ∫ speed dt
    m_eq   = E_batt / (eta_eb H_u)
    fuel_corr = (m_fuel + m_eq) / rho_f per 100 km

The method is the linear correction of SAE J1711 and UN ECE R101 Annex 8: fuel is corrected in
proportion to the net battery energy over the run. Those procedures take the slope from a
regression over several tests; here it is fixed by a stated engine-to-battery efficiency
`eta_eb` instead (assumed).

`P_stored` is the power out of the battery's store, `E i` behind the series resistance, not the
terminal power `v i`. A bench forms it as `meter.P_stored = drive.battery.E * drive.battery.i`.
For `Vehicle.Electric.Battery`, with constant `E`, its integral is `E Q_nom (SoC0 - SoC)`, so a
run that returns SoC to its start reports `E_batt = 0` and corrected fuel equal to raw fuel
exactly. Terminal energy would not: it falls short of that by `∫ R0 i^2 dt` on every run, and
would credit the car with fuel for its own resistive loss. `E_batt` is positive when the run
ends with less charge than it started, so a run that drew on the battery reports more corrected
fuel than raw fuel, and one that charged it reports less.

The integrals start at zero at t = 0, so every output reads 0 there. The per-100-km outputs
divide by `sqrt(s^2 + d_reg^2)` in place of `s`, which keeps the division finite at standstill
without an event. Until the car has covered many `d_reg` they are totals spread over that
length and mean nothing; at the end of a WLTC (23.3 km) the guard changes them by 1e-9 of their
value. Read them at the end of the run.

Fuel constants are the course's petrol: `rho_f` 0.745 kg/L (Hands-on 02) and `H_u` 43.4 MJ/kg
(Lecture 2 tasks, textbook), as in the Lecture 4 comparison of the BEV with the engine car.
"""
component SoCCorrectedFuel
  "Fuel mass flow into the engine [kg/s]"
  mdot_fuel = RealInput() {^mdot_fuel}
  "Power out of the battery's store, E i, positive discharging [W]"
  P_stored = RealInput() {^P_stored}
  "Vehicle speed along its path [m/s]"
  speed = RealInput() {^speed}
  "Raw fuel consumption [L/100 km]"
  fuel_raw = RealOutput() {^fuel_raw}
  "Net energy out of the battery's store since t = 0, positive when charge was drawn [MJ]"
  E_batt_MJ = RealOutput() {^E_batt_MJ}
  "SoC-corrected fuel consumption [L/100 km]"
  fuel_corr = RealOutput() {^fuel_corr}
  "SoC-corrected fuel energy, fuel_corr at H_u [MJ/100 km]"
  energy_corr = RealOutput() {^energy_corr}

  "Engine-to-battery efficiency, fuel energy to stored battery energy: 34.7 % on the Lecture 2 engine's best-BSFC line at 15 kW (238.75 g/kWh), a part-load charging point, times 0.90 for machine and inverter generating (inside ORNL's 0.80-0.96 combined band) and 0.97 for the battery's charging loss (derived; the 232 g/kWh best point would give 0.31, a bound that favors draining the battery, and charging further down the line costs more)"
  parameter eta_eb::Real = 0.30
  "Petrol lower heating value (Lecture 2 tasks, textbook)"
  parameter H_u::SpecificEnergy = 43.4e6
  "Petrol density, 0.745 kg/L (Hands-on 02)"
  parameter rho_f::Density = 745.0
  "Distance that regularizes the division by distance at standstill (assumed)"
  parameter d_reg::Length = 1.0

  "Fuel burned since t = 0"
  variable m_fuel::Mass
  "Net energy out of the battery's store since t = 0"
  variable E_batt::Energy
  "Distance driven since t = 0"
  variable s::Length
  "Fuel that would put E_batt back through the engine and the machine"
  variable m_eq::Mass
  "Regularized distance, s away from standstill"
  variable d::Length
relations
  initial m_fuel = 0.0
  initial E_batt = 0.0
  initial s = 0.0
  der(m_fuel) = mdot_fuel
  der(E_batt) = P_stored
  der(s) = speed
  m_eq = E_batt / (eta_eb * H_u)
  d = sqrt(s ^ 2 + d_reg ^ 2)
  # 1e8: m^3 to L (1e3) over m to 100 km (1e-5).
  fuel_raw = 1e8 * m_fuel / (rho_f * d)
  fuel_corr = fuel_raw + 1e8 * m_eq / (rho_f * d)
  energy_corr = 1e-9 * fuel_corr * rho_f * H_u
  E_batt_MJ = 1e-6 * E_batt
metadata {
  "_links": {
    "mdot_fuel": {"Dyad": {"placement": {"icon": {"x1": -50, "y1": 150, "x2": 50, "y2": 250}}}},
    "P_stored": {"Dyad": {"placement": {"icon": {"x1": -50, "y1": 450, "x2": 50, "y2": 550}}}},
    "speed": {"Dyad": {"placement": {"icon": {"x1": -50, "y1": 750, "x2": 50, "y2": 850}}}},
    "fuel_raw": {"Dyad": {"placement": {"icon": {"x1": 950, "y1": 100, "x2": 1050, "y2": 200}}}},
    "E_batt_MJ": {"Dyad": {"placement": {"icon": {"x1": 950, "y1": 333, "x2": 1050, "y2": 433}}}},
    "fuel_corr": {"Dyad": {"placement": {"icon": {"x1": 950, "y1": 566, "x2": 1050, "y2": 666}}}},
    "energy_corr": {"Dyad": {"placement": {"icon": {"x1": 950, "y1": 800, "x2": 1050, "y2": 900}}}}
  }
}
end

"""
Constant fuel flow, stored-power draw and speed into `SoCCorrectedFuel`, so that every integral
is a product a test can work out by hand. Defaults: 1 g/s of fuel, 1 kW drawn from the battery
and 20 m/s (assumed test inputs).
"""
test component TestSoCCorrectedFuel
  "Fuel mass flow (assumed test input)"
  parameter mdot::MassFlowRate = 1e-3
  "Power out of the battery's store, positive discharging (assumed test input)"
  parameter P::Power = 1000.0
  "Vehicle speed (assumed test input)"
  parameter v_car::Velocity = 20.0
  fuel = BlockComponents.Sources.Constant(k = mdot)
  battery = BlockComponents.Sources.Constant(k = P)
  motion = BlockComponents.Sources.Constant(k = v_car)
  meter = VehicleSystemsComponents.Vehicle.SoCCorrectedFuel()
relations
  connect(fuel.y, meter.mdot_fuel)
  connect(battery.y, meter.P_stored)
  connect(motion.y, meter.speed)
end

"Constant inputs for 500 s: 10 km at the bench's 20 m/s (derived)."
analysis SoCCorrectedFuelTransient
  extends TransientAnalysis(stop = 500.0, abstol = 1e-10, reltol = 1e-10)
  model = TestSoCCorrectedFuel()
end

"""
A real `Vehicle.Electric.Battery` (Leaf defaults, R0 = 0.1 Ohm) driven by a current source
through whole periods of a sine, so its charge, and SoC, return to the start while `R0 i^2` is
burned throughout. The battery's `E i` feeds `SoCCorrectedFuel` beside a constant fuel flow and
speed. `E_R0` and `E_dc` meter the resistive loss and the terminal energy for comparison.
"""
test component TestSoCCorrectedFuelBattery
  "Fuel mass flow (assumed test input)"
  parameter mdot::MassFlowRate = 1e-3
  "Vehicle speed (assumed test input)"
  parameter v_car::Velocity = 20.0
  "Discharge current amplitude (assumed test input)"
  parameter I_amp::Current = 100.0
  "Current waveform frequency, five periods in the 500 s run (assumed test input)"
  parameter f::Frequency = 0.01
  fuel = BlockComponents.Sources.Constant(k = mdot)
  motion = BlockComponents.Sources.Constant(k = v_car)
  wave = BlockComponents.Sources.Sine(amplitude = I_amp, frequency = f)
  load = ElectricalComponents.Analog.Sources.CurrentSource()
  battery = VehicleSystemsComponents.Vehicle.Electric.Battery()
  ground = ElectricalComponents.Analog.Basic.Ground()
  meter = VehicleSystemsComponents.Vehicle.SoCCorrectedFuel()
  "Energy burned in the battery's series resistance"
  variable E_R0::Energy
  "Net energy out of the battery terminals"
  variable E_dc::Energy
relations
  initial E_R0 = 0.0
  initial E_dc = 0.0
  connect(wave.y, load.I)
  connect(battery.p, load.p)
  connect(load.n, battery.n, ground.g)
  connect(fuel.y, meter.mdot_fuel)
  connect(motion.y, meter.speed)
  meter.P_stored = battery.E * battery.i
  der(E_R0) = battery.R0 * battery.i ^ 2
  der(E_dc) = battery.v * battery.i
end

"Five whole periods of the battery current, 500 s (derived)."
analysis SoCCorrectedFuelBatteryTransient
  extends TransientAnalysis(stop = 500.0, abstol = 1e-10, reltol = 1e-10)
  model = TestSoCCorrectedFuelBattery()
end
